spans.s:
Puṇḍarīka,
(1) n. of a locality: Māy 〔91〕;
(2) v.l. for Pauṇḍarīka, 2, q.v., n. of a former Buddha.

Puṇyaprabha,
(1) n. of a monk, disciple of Śākyamuni: Gv 〔47.9〕;
(2) n. of a lay-disciple: Gv 〔51.10〕.

Puṇyābha,
(1) n. of a Buddha: Mmk 〔305.13〕; 〔426.7〕 (both times following Amitābha in lists);
(2) n. of a god or class of gods: Mmk 〔19.10〕 (a nonce-form, invented here? cf. śuddhābha).
